{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941042-copying-a-book-with-matter-2e","id":941042,"title":"Copying a book with Matter [2e]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-31T22:31:18-07:00","id":941042,"title":"Copying a book with Matter [2e]","content":"Though a book holds a lot of information, at its core it's essentially just a large chunk of wood-pulp slices with ink in a specific pattern. So at first glance it <i>seems</i> like matter should be able to duplicate it. My question is how?<br /> <br /> At what level do you need Matter to copy a book if you had say, an empty book and some ink? (thats essentially just a &quot;control&quot; and moving the ink around)<br /> Do you need to know the information (i.e. read the book) first? Or would magic just take care of it if the Imago was &quot;make this one just like that one&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T23:56:09-07:00","id":941074,"title":"","content":"Yeah, having all the necessary materials at hand is a simple Ruling spell. You don't even need to know the content, as you say the spell will take care of everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T10:05:59-07:00","id":942037,"title":"","content":"To me it sounds a little more like a Weaving spell. A Ruling spell is not that &quot;smart&quot; as most of the examples require you giving a simple order. Perhaps Ruling with +1 Reach to make a book copy itself (an example of a complex task)? But then you have to take the time it would take to do so into account in the Duration of the spell. I feel Weaving would be the simplest way to do it, as its kind of a reconfiguration which aligns it to other Weaving spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T10:13:09-07:00","id":942043,"title":"","content":"I'd say that, if you're consciously commanding the ink into the right shape, it's Ruling. If you want it to just make a copy without needing to worry about it, it's Weaving. Same theory as the difference between puppeteering a corpse and making a zombie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:22:41-07:00","id":942151,"title":"","content":"Weaving would turn a blank book and some ink into a copy of another book, yeah. Patterning could turn a block of wood or whathaveyou into an exact copy of a book. Ruling could do it, but it'd be a pain in the ass and basically reproduce the actual process of making the book. You'd have to bind the pages, set the ink into the paper, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}